{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U8"],
      "pins": ["U8.4", "U8.5"],
      "nets": ["I2C4_SCL_NAVC", "I2C4_SDA_NAVC"],
      "observed": "On the NAVC Peripherals sheet the IIS2MDCTR magnetometer U8 has its SCL/SPC pin (4) wired to net I2C4_SCL_NAVC and its SDA/SDI/SDO pin (5) wired to net I2C4_SDA_NAVC. These two nets appear only on U8: no pin of NAVC1 (STM32F405RGTx) carries an I2C4 label (the MCU exposes I2C1 on PB6/PB7, I2C2 on PB8-PB11 and I2C3 on PA8/PA9), and the I2C pull-up network on the NAVC sheet (R28-R31, 4k7) pulls up only I2C1_*_NAVC and I2C2_*_NAVC. Every other NAVC sensor (BMI088 U5, TMP100 U6, MPRLS U7, EEPROM U9) is on I2C1_*_NAVC.",
      "expected": "The magnetometer must sit on the same I2C sensor bus as the other NAVC peripherals (I2C1_*_NAVC, which has both the MCU master and the 4k7 pull-ups R28/R29). The STM32F405 has no I2C4 peripheral, so an I2C4_*_NAVC net cannot be driven by the MCU and, lacking pull-ups, cannot function as an I2C bus at all.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "NAVC Peripherals sheet: U8 IIS2MDCTR pin 4 = 'I2C4_SCL_NAVC', pin 5 = 'I2C4_SDA_NAVC'; U5/U6/U7/U9 pins = 'I2C1_SCL_NAVC'/'I2C1_SDA_NAVC'; pull-ups R28-R31 4k7 on I2C1/I2C2 only; NAVC1 = 'STM32F405RGTx'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Component table: 'Magnetometer | NAVCPeripherals | ST IIS2MDCTR, I2C addr 0x1E'; §4: '3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs'"}
      ],
      "impact": "The magnetometer's I2C lines connect to a net that reaches no MCU pin and has no pull-ups, so U8 can never be addressed; the heading/magnetic data required by the navigation solution is lost (the INT_MAG_NAVC interrupt line is still wired to PA6, confirming the device was meant to be active).",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power stage, INA219 sense path, both MCUs, the FCC/NAVC link and the documented barometer RESET/EOC swap all match the specification; the one deviation I can read off the drawing is that the IIS2MDCTR magnetometer U8 is tied to an I2C4_*_NAVC net that the STM32F405 does not have and that has no pull-ups, unlike every other NAVC sensor which is on I2C1, leaving the magnetometer disconnected from the bus."
}

